1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,465
In this lesson, you'll set up automatic
appointment reminders by email and text.

2
00:00:05,465 --> 00:00:08,320
It's one of the simplest
changes you can make,

3
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:11,423
and one of the most effective
at cutting no-shows.

4
00:00:12,275 --> 00:00:13,984
Most no-shows aren't rude.

5
00:00:13,984 --> 00:00:15,364
People simply forget.

6
00:00:15,364 --> 00:00:19,899
A reminder the day before, and a
short text a couple of hours before,

7
00:00:19,899 --> 00:00:21,148
fixes most of that.

8
00:00:21,148 --> 00:00:24,040
Reminders are included
from the Growth plan.

9
00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:26,800
Open your calendar from Calendar Settings.

10
00:00:27,649 --> 00:00:30,435
Go to Notifications
and Additional Options.

11
00:00:30,435 --> 00:00:35,554
At the top are the notifications that go
out when something happens: a booking,

12
00:00:35,554 --> 00:00:37,627
a reschedule, or a cancellation.

13
00:00:37,627 --> 00:00:40,089
Each one uses a template you can edit.

14
00:00:40,089 --> 00:00:44,431
Keep them short and friendly, and
always include your phone number.

15
00:00:45,281 --> 00:00:50,186
Below those are reminders, which are
sent a set time before the appointment.

16
00:00:50,186 --> 00:00:53,607
This calendar already sends
an email 24 hours before,

17
00:00:53,607 --> 00:00:55,801
and a text message 2 hours before.

18
00:00:55,801 --> 00:01:00,255
Each one goes out automatically,
timed to that patient's appointment.

19
00:01:01,105 --> 00:01:05,032
New patients often need to bring
forms and their medical history,

20
00:01:05,032 --> 00:01:07,993
so let's add one more
reminder, a little earlier.

21
00:01:07,993 --> 00:01:10,772
Click Add reminder, and
choose how to send it.

22
00:01:10,772 --> 00:01:13,854
We'll use email, because
there's a bit more to say.

23
00:01:14,705 --> 00:01:17,498
Choose when it goes out: 48 hours before.

24
00:01:17,498 --> 00:01:19,065
Then write the message.

25
00:01:19,065 --> 00:01:23,835
The words in curly brackets are
custom values, so each patient's name,

26
00:01:23,835 --> 00:01:26,764
appointment and time
fill in automatically.

27
00:01:26,764 --> 00:01:30,920
Mention what to bring, and how
to reschedule if plans change.

28
00:01:31,770 --> 00:01:35,965
Click Add reminder, and the
calendar now sends three reminders.

29
00:01:35,965 --> 00:01:41,492
If the patient cancels or reschedules,
Kyntlo stops or moves the reminders for you,

30
00:01:41,492 --> 00:01:45,821
so nobody is reminded about an
appointment that no longer exists.

31
00:01:46,670 --> 00:01:51,420
One important rule: only text people
who've agreed to receive messages.

32
00:01:51,420 --> 00:01:55,501
That's why the booking form from
lesson 5.3 asks for consent.

33
00:01:55,501 --> 00:01:59,648
And contacts marked Do Not Disturb
never receive texts at all.

34
00:01:59,648 --> 00:02:04,666
Respecting that keeps your number in
good standing with the phone networks.

35
00:02:05,518 --> 00:02:10,103
Click Save, and every future booking
on this calendar gets these reminders

36
00:02:10,103 --> 00:02:10,970
automatically.

37
00:02:10,970 --> 00:02:14,006
Repeat the same steps for
each of your calendars.

38
00:02:14,006 --> 00:02:18,901
Reminders work for appointments you book
by hand too, not just online bookings.

39
00:02:19,750 --> 00:02:24,204
Want more control, like a different
message for first-time patients,

40
00:02:24,204 --> 00:02:26,496
or a text asking people to confirm?

41
00:02:26,496 --> 00:02:28,985
Build reminders as a workflow instead.

42
00:02:28,985 --> 00:02:33,438
Bloom already has one called
"Appointment Confirmation & Reminders",

43
00:02:33,438 --> 00:02:36,124
and you'll learn to build it in Module 9.

44
00:02:36,984 --> 00:02:38,086
Here's a pro tip.

45
00:02:38,086 --> 00:02:40,291
Two or three reminders are plenty.

46
00:02:40,291 --> 00:02:45,348
One the day before, so people can
rearrange, and one a couple of hours before,

47
00:02:45,348 --> 00:02:46,061
as a nudge.

48
00:02:46,061 --> 00:02:49,822
Any more starts to feel like
nagging, and people tune out.

49
00:02:50,672 --> 00:02:52,478
That's the end of Module 5!

50
00:02:52,478 --> 00:02:56,692
You can now take bookings, deposits
and reminders on autopilot.

51
00:02:56,692 --> 00:03:00,505
Next, in Module 6, we'll track
every deal with pipelines.

52
00:03:00,505 --> 00:03:01,442
See you there.
